  "final_message": "Done. Summary of the implementation:\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`) \u2014 Flask + SQLite at `./data/app.db` (auto-created, survives restarts):\n- `POST /api/auth/register` (201), `POST /api/auth/login` (200 + `{token}`), bearer-token auth (401 without), admin account `admin` upserted from `ADMIN_PASSWORD` at startup (sign-in disabled when unset/empty, name reserved at registration)\n- Reservations CRUD with ownership isolation (others' reservations 404), `notes` cleared when omitted on PUT, per-slot capacity of 20 with atomic check-and-write (`BEGIN IMMEDIATE`) so refused bookings/changes change nothing and an edited reservation's own seats aren't double-counted; `GET /api/reservations` (filter by `date`, earliest first), `GET /api/availability?date` (only slots with bookings, `booked`/`remaining`), `GET /api/admin/reservations` (`date`, `page`, `page_size` \u2192 items/total/page/page_size), `GET /api/health`. Full-slot refusals answer 400 with `\"Slot is fully booked\"`.\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`, React + TS + Vite + Tailwind v4, only `src/index.css` as Tailwind entry): sign-in/register panel with sign-out and username in the header, shared day picker with booked slots/remaining seats (progress bars), booking form surfacing API messages (incl. full slot), my-reservations grouped by date with inline edit and a two-step cancel confirmation, and an admin panel listing every reservation of the chosen day with the guest total and pagination.\n\n**Notes**: `backend/requirements.txt` now carries the full pinned+hashed install set (flask, gunicorn + closure) \u2014 pip treats hashed constraints as requiring hash-checking mode, so the Dockerfile's `pip install -r \u2026 -c \u2026` only works this way (verified with pip 24.0/25.1/25.1.1). Verified end-to-end with gunicorn: auth flows, capacity rules, notes clearing, admin paging, SPA serving, and restart persistence; `npm ci && npm run build` and `tsc --noEmit` pass.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
